<section>
    <h2>Files go both ways</h2>
    <p>
        Real apps hand you files (invoices, exports, reports) and ask for them (avatars, CSVs, attachments). A test
        can't look in your Downloads folder or click around the system file picker, and it doesn't need to:
        Playwright catches the download before it lands, and fills a file input directly.
    </p>
</section>

<section>
    <h2>Catching a download</h2>
    <p>A download is an event, so start waiting for it before the click that causes it:</p>
<pre><code>import fs from 'node:fs/promises';

const downloadPromise = page.waitForEvent('download');
await page.getByRole('link', { name: 'Export' }).click();
const download = await downloadPromise;

console.log(download.suggestedFilename());              // the name the server gave it
const text = await fs.readFile(await download.path(), 'utf8');   // where it was saved
await download.saveAs('exports/report.csv');             // keep a copy</code></pre>
    <p class="tip">
        <strong>Wait first, click second.</strong> Don't <code>await</code> the promise before the click: start it,
        click, then await it. Otherwise the download can come and go before you begin listening.
    </p>
</section>

<section>
    <h2>Uploading</h2>
    <p>
        <code>setInputFiles()</code> fills a file input. Give it a path, several paths, or a file made in memory,
        so your test doesn't need a fixtures folder:
    </p>
<pre><code>const upload = page.getByLabel('Attachment');

await upload.setInputFiles('fixtures/avatar.png');
await upload.setInputFiles({
  name: 'notes.txt',                       // the name the page sees
  mimeType: 'text/plain',
  buffer: Buffer.from('Hello from a test'),
});
await upload.setInputFiles([]);            // clear it again</code></pre>
    <p>
        When a button opens the picker and the input is hidden, catch the picker instead:
    </p>
<pre><code>const chooserPromise = page.waitForEvent('filechooser');
await page.getByRole('button', { name: 'Upload' }).click();
const chooser = await chooserPromise;
await chooser.setFiles('fixtures/avatar.png');</code></pre>
</section>

<section>
    <h2>The Courier's Counter</h2>
    <p>
        The Guild trusts paper, not screens. Collect your sealed dispatch, read the seal inside it, and hand back a
        reply with the seal in it, in a file with exactly the name the dispatch asks for. Ten seconds.
    </p>
</section>
